sentences.text:
. 
Let the petitioners be released on bail, in the event of his arrest or surrender before the Sub-ordinate court within a period of four weeks from the receipt of this order, on furnishing bail bond of Rs.25,000/-(Rupees Twenty Five Thousand) each with two sureties of the like amount each in connection with Ahiyapur P.S. Case No. 537 of 2022 to the satisfaction of learned learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Muzaffarpur, subject to the conditions as laid down under Section 438(2) of the Cr.P.C. with further conditions that:
(i) the petitioners will make themselves available to the police as and when required in course of investigation;
(ii) the petitioners shall appear on each and every date before the Trial court and failure to do so for two consecutive dates without plausible reason will entail cancellation of their bail bond by the Trial court itself;
(iii) the petitioners shall in no way try to induce or promise or threat the witnesses or tamper with the evidences, failing which the State shall be at liberty to take steps for cancellation of the bail bonds;
(iv) the petitioners shall desist from committing any criminal offence again failing which the State shall be at liberty Patna High Court CR.

